    {
     "t": "list",
     "items": [
      "**A title and a copy are different things: the title is searched and reserved, the copy is borrowed.** Why: it is the first modelling call, and it is what makes reservations possible later.",
      "**The borrower and due date live on the Copy; there is no Loan class.** Why: one place for each fact, and four small classes carry the whole design.",
      "**Every rule sits in the Library: the loan length, the limit and the fine, and the fine is its own helper.** Why: a per-member fine changes one function and nothing else.",
      "**Today's date is a parameter, so the same input gives the same due date and fine.** Why: you can trace a demo by hand, and a test needs no fake clock.",
      "**Check-free and set-borrower happen as one step, or two desks can both borrow the same copy.** Why: it is the senior signal: the concurrency answer, not only the happy path.",
      "**No Librarian class, no LoanFactory, no Singleton for the library.** Why: nothing in the scope uses them."
     ]
    }
